{"title":"2001 OIM Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the maximum number of increasing arithmetic progressions of three terms that can have a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5214ae0e0ea07dc3f4fa0d3b0fc04e7e0b7e6e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> real numbers.\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> Three terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/30853e201687b2c6f42173da84420e168999a6d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i, a_j , a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" /> of a sequence of real numbers form an increasing arithmetic progression if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785490c57a3e354acbae25356406803870542caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; a_j &lt; a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7281abfc6a494b2636144ed535bd6b992c0dab32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j - a_i = a_k - a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 41/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 949/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.765      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    5.765      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26161:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195430 and revision id 207223. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}